course: dictionary
lesson: 15131
title: Saturated: soaked, full and strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Saturated can mean different things, so the clues in the sentence help you choose. Its simplest meaning is soaked. «After the storm, the grass was completely saturated.» The clues are storm and completely: the grass has taken in so much water that it cannot hold any more.
explain: Science uses saturated in a special way. «Stir salt into the water until no more will dissolve. Now the solution is saturated.» The clues are stir, no more and dissolve. The water is so full of dissolved salt that no more can fit in.
explain: Other places use it too. On food labels you may see «saturates», which means saturated fat. «The car park was saturated, with no space left for another car» means it was so full that there was no room for more. Always check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Saturated means completely soaked with water or another liquid.
fact: In science, a saturated solution has so much dissolved in it that no more can dissolve.
fact: Saturated fat is found mostly in butter, cheese and fatty meat, and eating too much is not good for the heart.
fact: A saturated market or place is so full of something that there is no room for more.
fact: A saturated colour is strong and bright.
fact: Saturate is the verb, and saturated is its past form, as in «The rain saturated the field».
exercise: «The sponge was saturated after the spill.» What does saturated mean here? | Dried out in the sun | Very small and light | Cut into thin slices | *Completely soaked with liquid
exercise: «The science teacher said the salt water was saturated.» What does this tell us? | The salt has all gone and nothing is left | *No more salt can dissolve in it | The water is boiling hot
exercise: «The painting used saturated reds and blues.» What does saturated suggest about the colours? | Dull and grey | Pale and faded | Hidden under paint | *Strong and bright
test: Which food label would show saturates, and which food might have saturated fat? | *Cheese | Lettuce | Glass of water | Apple
test: Which sentence uses saturated to mean full, with no room for more? | The sky was a saturated blue. | *The car park was saturated, with no space left for another car. | The sponge was saturated with water. | The jumper was saturated, so it felt heavy and cold.
exam: What is a saturated solution? | Water with no salt in it at all | A solution that has been frozen solid | *A liquid with so much dissolved in it that no more can dissolve | A cloudy mixture of sand and water
